Babet 2.7.0 roadmap
====================

[x] Define the standalone compressed-stream API outside babet.archive.
[x] Add secure gzip/xz/bzip2/zstd compression and automatic decompression.
[x] Add pinned sources, bounded output, concatenated-member support, atomic
    publication, strict Lua validation, worker registration, tests, and FR/EN
    documentation for the first compression lot.
[x] Add strictly validated format-specific compression levels.
[x] Extend archive creation to accept an explicit source list.
[x] Define deterministic archive entry names, duplicate/collision handling,
    absolute-path policy, and symlink rules for explicit source lists.
[x] Add include/exclude rules backed by the bounded safe glob engine.
[x] Audit code, tests, FR/EN documentation, examples and PDF manuals before
    release, using the same standard as 2.6.0.

Deferred ideas retained in notes.md:
- parent-side PATH resolution followed by execve;
- worker-to-worker channels;
- cooperative cancellation design;
- macOS/BSD portability.
